  "id": "COMPOUND:20118 - PROTEIN:6000",
  "verbalization": "Selaginellin A is implicated in the interaction with Lysosomal phospholipase A2 through multiple pathways, with the Prostaglandin E2 receptor EP4 subtype acting as a common intermediate. This receptor is targeted by Selaginellin A, which in turn influences the activity of Sagittine B and Sinuflexibilin, both of which ultimately affect Lysosomal phospholipase A2. The evidence suggests a potential mechanism where Selaginellin A modulates signaling through the EP4 receptor, leading to the activation of downstream targets that influence lysosomal phospholipase A2 activity. The varying scores across the paths indicate a degree of confidence in this relationship, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The presence of multiple pathways converging on Lysosomal phospholipase A2 highlights the complexity of the biological processes involved, and further experimental validation would be necessary to confirm the direct relationship.",
